  "summary": "Full assessment of all 137 English/Vietnamese passages and both titles. The moonlit evening, Sister Sara, the man-free streets, the reversal of purdah, Sara’s house and garden, the sun-heat and water-balloon inventions, the war won by science and the men’s retreat into the mardana, religion and sacred relations, the air-car, the Queen and the waking are complete and in order. The separate-context pass found no major issue; seventeen minor findings were revised, including the arms pun. Fidelity, voice, imagery and mechanics are 9.0, naturalness 8.5. Unrounded weighted score 8.925 meets the unchanged 8.6 threshold. No unresolved major or critical issue remains.",
